date:e-e6875b00d9664ca7a1b3bd00","relation":{"from":"Spice","relation":"causes","to":"spicy"},"required_source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3"]}],"prompt_version":"p2-assessor-production-v9","replay_ancestry":[{"root":"954ed2bb-b2fb-4b83-adc1-509f12901c99","source_slot":"s0"},{"root":"323122d9-1828-4260-8512-4674f0971470","source_slot":"s1"}],"schema_version":"p2-assessor-v6","source_purpose_mask":["external_evidence","model_output"],"sources":[{"available":true,"role":"model_output","slot":"s0","source_id":"954ed2bb-b2fb-4b83-adc1-509f12901c99","text":"I have a few ingredients, mixed preferences, and no reliable recipe for tonight. How would you improvise a meal?"},{"available":true,"role":"model_output","slot":"s1","source_id":"323122d9-1828-4260-8512-4674f0971470","text":"Since you have some ingredients and preferences, but no specific recipe, how about we improvise? Could you tell me what ingredients you currently have on hand and what kinds of flavors or textures you're craving right now (like spicy, savory, or sweet)? Knowing those details will help me suggest a few creative combinations! 😊"},{"available":true,"role":"external","slot":"s2","source_id":"446033b2-8ee4-4c88-9193-2d0a3fd10ea9","text":"I have some chicken, bell peppers, and onions. I'm craving something a bit spicy but not too hot. How can we make that work?"},{"available":true,"role":"model_output","slot":"s3","source_id":"1016c05a-4edc-4093-a2f7-e438d4334726","text":"That sounds like a great starting point! With chicken, bell peppers, and onions, we can definitely whip up something delicious.\n\nSince you're looking for something a little spicy but not overly hot, how about a **Spicy Chicken and Veggie Stir-Fry**?\n\nHere is a quick idea:\n1. **Sauté the Onions and Peppers:** Sauté the chopped onions and bell peppers until they are soft and fragrant.\n2. **Cook the Chicken:** Cook your chicken until it's fully cooked.\n3. **The Spice:** Instead of high-level heat, we'll use the \"spicy\" element subtly. We can add a small amount of chili flakes or a tiny bit of cayenne pepper if you have it, but keep the heat low.\n4. **Assembly:** Toss everything together in one pan and let it simmer briefly to let the flavors blend.\n\n**How does that sound? Would you like to make a stir-fry, or perhaps something like a simple pan-seared chicken dish with a side of peppers?**"}]},"resolved":[{"provenance":{"ancestry":[{"root":"323122d9-1828-4260-8512-4674f0971470","source_slot":"s1"}],"applicable_categories":["replay_linked"],"corresponding_source_slots":["s1","s3"],"credit_eligible":false,"dependence":"replay_linked","monitor_id":"candidate:e-5911a3a011ad5bcf00fcedbb","provenance_group_keys":["replay:323122d9-1828-4260-8512-4674f0971470"],"resolution_reason":"runtime_source_role_and_recorded_ancestry","schema_version":"p2-provenance-v1"},"semantic":{"corresponding_source_slots":["s1","s3"],"coverage":{"complete":true,"reason":null,"source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3"]},"evidence":{"end":755,"quote":"**Assembly:** Toss everything together in one pan and let it simmer briefly to let the flavors blend.","source_slot":"s3","start":654},"expression_status":"unknown","monitor_id":"candidate:e-5911a3a011ad5bcf00fcedbb","relation_support":"unsupported","status":"present"}},{"provenance":{"ancestry":[],"applicable_categories":["no_identified_link"],"corresponding_source_slots":["s3"],"credit_eligible":false,"dependence":"no_identified_link","monitor_id":"candidate:e-e6875b00d9664ca7a1b3bd00","provenance_group_keys":[],"resolution_reason":"runtime_source_role_and_recorded_ancestry","schema_version":"p2-provenance-v1"},"semantic":{"corresponding_source_slots":["s3"],"coverage":{"complete":true,"reason":null,"source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3"]},"evidence":{"end":537,"quote":"**The Spice:** Instead of high-level heat, we'll use the \"spicy\" element subtly.","source_slot":"s3","start":457},"expression_status":"unknown","monitor_id":"candidate:e-e6875b00d9664ca7a1b3bd00","relation_support